=== layout: one-panel

# [*Steps in Unordered Tetrad Mapping*]{color=#000000}

@body

- 1. [Read the parental genotypes from the cross.]{color=#D40000}
- 2. [Pick two genes; classify each tetrad as PD, NPD, or TT.]{color=#B74300}
  - With three genes, keep all loci visible.
- 3. [Compare PD and NPD to test linkage.]{color=#6C6C00}
- 4. [Calculate map distance for linked genes.]{color=#007A00}
  - Add half the TT count and three times the NPD count.
  - Divide by the total tetrads; multiply by 100 for cM.
- 5. [Repeat for every pair in a three-gene problem.]{color=#003FFF}
- 6. [Choose the middle gene and draw the map.]{color=#A719DB}

